A||||7||MrFieroUK||Caddy aluminum small block||||5||
Z||000000||MrFieroUK||11-08-2001||11:43 PM||||Any one got the tech. specs. for the 4.5/4.9 OHV aluminum caddy small block - can't find anything useful on the www.<P>Bore/stroke: cam duration/lift/overlap: lifter type roller/flat: power & torque @ rpms: engine ecu type: dizzy or DIS:TBI/PFI/SEFI:wieght dry/wet:etc., etc.<P>Literature on rebuilds?<BR>Thanx.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-09-2001||07:27 AM||||4.9 liters, 300 ci, overhead valve, 90degree V8, aluminum block, iron heads, iron boreliners, 200hp@4400rpm, 275lbft@3000rpm, 9.5:1 compression, bore 92mm-3.63", stroke 92mm-3.62", rocker arm ratio 1.60:1, hydraulic roller lifters, Valve timing: intake opens 21* btdc - closes 257* atdc, exhaust opens 245* btdc - closes 29* atdc. Valve lift: intake 9.75mm exhaust 10.06mm, duration: intake 278* exhaust 274*, overlap 49*, Igniton- HEI coil-in-cap distributor, sequential port fuel injection, 371 lbs dry with starter,alternator, and A/C.<P>Rebuilding info can be found on my website: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/caderoinfo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/caderoinfo.htm</A> <P>Is that good enough?||||reg||7
Z||000002||mrfixit58||11-09-2001||08:03 AM||||Jon,<P>The best part of your post is that now we have all this critical information in ONE location.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||Master_Sushi||11-09-2001||11:09 AM||||Whats the RPM range on them?||||reg||5
Z||000004||rockcrawl||11-09-2001||04:02 PM||||The engine seems to make good even power up until about 4500RPM, after that it falls off pretty sharply. Most if not all of the stock ECMs limit the revs to 4500. I have mine set at 6000. Someone once said that after 4500RPM the engine is just making noise, I must agree. Several of us are seeing what can be done in the way of a reground cam to wake this thing up a little. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrFieroUK||11-11-2001||11:51 AM||||Thanks Rockcrawl - do you happen to knoew if the 4.5 has an hydraulic roller cam?<P>Your help is appreciated||||reg||14
Z||000006||rockcrawl||11-11-2001||06:51 PM||||The 4.5 uses the same roller cam as the 4.9, but the 4.9 has new lifter guides with a new angle for improved camshaft stability. The 4.1 uses flat lifters. Some other changes for the introduction of the 4.9 in '91 include a new gerotor oil pump (33% decrease in pump drive loads, 13% increase in flow, 18% increase in pressure @ 2000rpm, and a 64% decrease in oil aeration), new oil pan and baffle for less chance of oil starvation, new profile on pistons for reduced cold noise (the 4.5 pistons are noticeably noisy when cold), new style crankshaft ballancer, as well as a few other minor changes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MrFieroUK||11-12-2001||01:24 PM||||Thanks Rockcrawl - My plans for a 3.2 ali-headed roller cam V6 just bit the dust! I'm Goin' Huntin' - continental Europe first - lots of choice in Holland and Germany... little or nothing in the UK. Later...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
